# Build context for the `frontend` service is the repo root (docker-compose.yml),
# so everything below would otherwise be shipped to the Docker daemon on every
# build. The frontend image only needs QT_FrontEnd/ and codex/.
#
# The `api` service has its own context (./QT_API) and its own .dockerignore.

# The API is not part of the frontend build - and this is what keeps the
# production secrets out of the frontend build context.
QT_API/
**/appsettings.Production.json
.env

# Runtime data and uploads (server-side only, never built)
**/App_Data/
**/uploads/

# Dependencies and build output - reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.angular/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# TLS material - Cloudflare terminates TLS, nothing here needs certs
**/ssl/
*.pem
*.key

# Tooling / editor noise
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
**/*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Docs - not needed to build either frontend
*.md
